/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A function returns its parameter from inside an If arm, and nowhere else.

    What a call hands back is as deep as the arguments its function may return. The only place
    this one returns its parameter is the BODY of an If arm; its other return is a top-level
    constant, which lives in no region. A walk that does not look inside an If arm finds nothing
    flowing to the return, takes the result to be in no region, and accepts this — and the compiled
    program then reads `inner` after the rabbit's Done. has freed it
    (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O1). */

Define blank as a series of number permanently.

Bind series of number to launder, given (the series of number s, the fact flag):
    If flag:
        Return s.
    Done.
    Return blank.
Done.

Define outer as a series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    outer becomes cast launder on (inner, true).
Done.
State outer.
